I haven't followed this thread closely, but one way of 'keeping track' is to
use a higher dimensional array. As Spencer says, a more complicated result
could be stored in a list, which could then be bound together using abind,
which is available on Statlib for Splus and as a package on CRAN for R.

do.call("abind",c(list.result,other.args.to.abind))

