However, I have a fisher.exact function for the 2x2 only, that looks 
like the following:

> fisher.exact
function(x, y = NULL)
{
  #       a | b
  #  x = -------
  #       c | d
  if(!is.null(y)) x <- table(x, y) else x <- round(x)
  a <- x[1, 1]
  b <- x[1, 2]
  c <- x[2, 1]
  d <- x[2, 2]
  N <- sum(x)
  p <- dhyper(a, a + b, c + d, a + c)
  x <- seq(max(0, a + b - (N - a - c)), min(a + b, a + c))
  dhyp <- dhyper(x, a + b, c + d, a + c)
  sum(dhyp[dhyp <= p])
}
> fisher.exact(m)
[1] 0.003818837
>

which returns the p-value (this matches the results from above). I'm not 
sure why there is a restriction in fisher.test.

